      "explanation": "The number of true statements about the emitted radiation is 2, i.e. statements (A) and (C).\n\n<br><br>(A) is True: The de-Broglie wavelength of an electron can be calculated as lambda = h / p, where h is Planck's constant and p is the momentum of the electron. The momentum of an electron with a velocity of 1000 m/s is mv, where m is the mass of an electron. Plugging in the values, we get \n<br><br><mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -11.278ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"48.71ex\" height=\"23.686ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -5484.7 21529.9 10469.4\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mtable\"><g data-mml-node=\"mtr\" transform=\"translate(0,4593)\"><g data-mml-node=\"mtd\"></g><g data-mml-node=\"mtd\"><g data-mml-node=\"mstyle\"><g data-mml-node=\"msub\"><g data-mml-node=\"TeXAtom\" data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"56\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-56\"></use></g></g><g data-mml-node=\"TeXAtom\" transform=\"translate(783,-150) scale(0.707)\" data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><g data-mml-node=\"TeXAtom\" data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"65\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-65\"></use></g></g></g></g><g data-mml-node=\"mo\" transform=\"translate(1424.7,0)\"><use data-c=\"3D\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-3D\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mn\" transform=\"translate(2480.5,0)\"><use data-c=\"31\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-31\"></use><use data-c=\"30\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-30\" transform=\"translate(500,0)\"></use><use data-c=\"30\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-30\" transform=\"translate(1000,0)\"></use><use data-c=\"30\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-30\" transform=\"translate(1500,0)\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"TeXAtom\" data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\" transform=\"translate(4480